Original commit body from 8d3a02b2e1cc68afaf7e7349ec7c315ce220357f:

method-call-recovery-linker resolves by class-hint-and-short-name with a
line-proximity tiebreaker and no receiver evidence. It was applying that to
unresolved calls whose producer had already stated WHERE the callee lives.

dst_ref with a module path is ADR-0035's complete external identity key,
stated positively or abstained per ADR-0057 §15.1. The pass that read the
imports and the scope made that claim; a short-name match is strictly less
evidence, so an in-repo answer CONTRADICTS it rather than filling a gap --
which is what §11 settles by keeping both edges and §14 declines to demote.
The linker now refuses outright, applying the same rule one stage earlier at
the pass that would otherwise manufacture the contest.

The refusal reads the unresolved edge the recovery was derived FROM, not the
call site: a.b(c.d()) puts two calls on one line and one sibling's claim says
nothing about the other. A site-keyed version would have refused 7 recoveries
whose own stub abstained.

Measured on a single-backend Python self-survey of this repository:

  method-call-recovery edges   92 -> 64   (28 removed, all wrong)
  precision                    51% -> 73%
  inherited-calls-linker       329 -> 329 (untouched)
  §14 demotions                0 -> 0

26 of the 28 targeted a dataclass FIELD -- tree_sitter_rust.language() bound
to Symbol.language (19 sites), id(stub) to Symbol.id, type(e).__name__ to
IpcPattern.type. The other 2 were os.environ.get -> TrackerSet.get and
pathlib.Path.exists -> TrackerSet.exists.

NOT asserted: that this linker is now correct. 17 of the remaining 64 are
still wrong, every one a receiver-blind mis-bind where the stub abstained and
no receiver_type_hint was stamped (0 of 90 audited Python stubs carried one).
Filed as WI-fihun, which also carries the callability-taxonomy question and
the two disagreeing hardcoded _CALLABLE_KINDS sets.

